From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Meir Dick <mdick85@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:46:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: Intel: sof_sdw: split a four-amp TAS2783A link into two
 PDIs

Four TAS2783A mono amplifiers aggregated on one SoundWire link cannot
be driven from a single two-channel PDI. The bus hands every peripheral
on the link the same pair of slots, so all four amplifiers play the
same channel and the machine has no stereo image at all.

Give the amplifier dai_link two CPU DAI pins instead of one. Two pins
select the sdca-2amp function topology, whose ALH multi-gateway copier
duplicates the stereo stream to both PDIs, and the bus then packs the
slots as [L, R, L, R] in codec-list order. Each amplifier takes its own
channel from its slot through .set_tdm_slot.

The split is confined to a playback link carrying exactly four TI
TAS2783A parts (vendor 0x0102, part 0x0000) on a single link, so no
other machine changes behaviour.

Depends on "soundwire: stream: append ports when a second DAI joins a
stream"; without it the second PDI overwrites the first port's
configuration and the link is silent.

Signed-off-by: Meir Dick <mdick85@gmail.com>
---
 sound/soc/intel/boards/sof_sdw.c | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/intel/boards/sof_sdw.c b/sound/soc/intel/boards/sof_sdw.c
index 60b4d86..e6e63f9 100644
--- a/sound/soc/intel/boards/sof_sdw.c
+++ b/sound/soc/intel/boards/sof_sdw.c
@@ -940,6 +940,7 @@ static int create_sdw_dailink(struct snd_soc_card *card,
 		struct snd_soc_dai_link_component *platform;
 		int num_cpus = hweight32(sof_dai->link_mask[stream]);
 		int num_codecs = sof_dai->num_devs[stream];
+		bool split_amp_pdis = false;
 		int playback, capture;
 		int cur_link = 0;
 		int i = 0, j = 0;
@@ -965,6 +966,26 @@ static int create_sdw_dailink(struct snd_soc_card *card,
 		if (!name)
 			return -ENOMEM;
 
+		/*
+		 * Four TAS2783A mono amplifiers aggregated on one SoundWire
+		 * link (HP EliteBook X G2i, board 8E86) cannot be driven from
+		 * a single 2ch PDI: the bus gives every peripheral the same
+		 * pair of slots, so all four play the same channel. Split them
+		 * across two CPU DAI pins. The ALH multi-gateway copier in the
+		 * resulting sdca-2amp topology duplicates the stereo stream to
+		 * both PDIs, and because the bus packs slots in codec-list
+		 * order - the match table lists the amplifiers L, R, L, R by
+		 * physical side - the slots come out [L, R, L, R] and each
+		 * amplifier's own channel mask selects its side.
+		 */
+		if (stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK && num_cpus == 1 &&
+		    num_codecs == 4 && sof_end->codec_info->vendor_id == 0x0102 &&
+		    sof_end->codec_info->part_id == 0x0000) {
+			split_amp_pdis = true;
+			num_cpus = 2;
+			dev_dbg(dev, "four-amp TAS2783A link: splitting into 2 PDIs\n");
+		}
+
 		cpus = devm_kcalloc(dev, num_cpus, sizeof(*cpus), GFP_KERNEL);
 		if (!cpus)
 			return -ENOMEM;
@@ -985,7 +1006,8 @@ static int create_sdw_dailink(struct snd_soc_card *card,
 			if (!sof_end->dai_info->direction[stream])
 				continue;
 
-			if (cur_link != sof_end->link_mask) {
+			if (cur_link != sof_end->link_mask ||
+			    (split_amp_pdis && j == 2)) {
 				int link_num = ffs(sof_end->link_mask) - 1;
 				int pin_num = intel_ctx->sdw_pin_index[link_num]++;
 
